        <h2 class="subhead" id="overview">Overview</h2>
        <div>
            This module takes a 1280x720p 60fps video stream as an input using the Xilinx RGB video format. Next it will crop the image to the desired shape, 
            then it will resize this cropped image to a 28x28 video stream. The cropping coordinates, and thus resizing ratio, can be changed dynamically by the user via the input pins. 
            The output will always be a 28x28 video stream. There are no restrictions on the shape or size of the sub-image rectangle.
            <br> <br>

            Dynamic input, fixed output. Low latency, low resource usage. As an enhancement, a few adjustments could be made to have dynamic input, dynamic output. <br> <br>

